text:
vaibhav: Heads-up 1 i'm opening a docs PR to tidy the model cards for sable6b and fjord4b. Need: CSV link fix, key rename, small migration snippets for SDK v3->v4, and an embeddings shard note. PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/4991
lina: thanks. we'll want to standardize on `max_sequence_length` (not `seq_limit`) and update the frontmatter schema in the card. i'll patch that in the PR.
marta: runtime gave preliminary ceilings: sable6b(fp16)=6144, sable6b-quant=4096, fjord4b(fp16)=8192, fjord4b-quant=6144. please prefix them with "variant-dependent" and link to data/model-catalog.csv for per-variant numbers.
vaibhav: good. also add a one-line benchmark row comparing q4_0 vs fp16 at batch sizes 1 and 16 and a footnote "results vary by GPU family and kernel selection".
lina: i'll add two compact snippets: 1) SDK v4 resolve+generate with a try/catch fallback to compat alias, 2) CLI curl example showing the compat alias. keep both short.
marta: small ops request 1 pause public deprecation flips for any legacy fjord aliases until ops confirms no pinned reservations. we had one customer last week using a pinned alias.
vaibhav: ack. PR will include the deprecation banner behind a feature flag and a TODO with the target flip date. we'll not flip until ops greenlights.
docs-bot: Deploy preview: https://deploy-preview.redwood-docs.io/pr-4991 (CI #12012) :eyes:
runtime: note: kernel selection can shift the effective ceiling by a few hundred tokens on some GPU families. Recommend wording: "effective ceilings may vary slightly by GPU family and kernel selection." marta: added that wording to the compatibility paragraph.
lina: pasting SDK snippet (compact) for review:
```js
// SDK v4: prefer quantized, fallback to compat alias
const variant = await client.models.findVariant('sable6b', { preferQuantized: true });
try {
  const out = await client.generate({ model: variant, input: prompt });
  console.log(out.generated_text);
} catch (err) {
  const fallback = 'sable6b-compat-q4_0';
  const out2 = await client.generate({ model: fallback, input: prompt });
  console.log(out2.generated_text);
}
```
vaibhav: looks good. can you also add the CLI alias example: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -d '{"model":"sable6b:compat-q4_0","input":"..."}'` and a one-line embedding snippet showing shard hint: `client.embed({model: variant, input: texts, shardCount: 8})` with note about shard sizing for large corpora.
marta: I'll also remove the hard-coded HTML table and add an include that pulls from data/model-catalog.csv so numbers stay in sync. leaving a TODO to hook the automation pipeline.
ci-bot: Preview build passed (CI #12012). accessibility checks OK.
lina: tiny nit: replace any `sequence_limit` keys in examples with `max_sequence_length` and remove trailing commas in JSON samples.
vaibhav: thanks all. plan: small edits now, wait for ops greenlight to flip banner, then merge. i'll open follow-up PR to sync the CSV -> generated table. ping here if ops asks to delay.
marta: monitoring ops. if they flag pinned instances i'll add the delay note. thanks!"
